<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morice Line</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1956">1956</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Morice Line was a fortified barrier built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1956 along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>'s border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, named after the defence minister André Morice. Made of electrified fences, minefields and radar, backed by mobile troops, it cut the FLN's fighters inside Algeria off from their bases and supplies in Tunisia. A similar line ran along the Moroccan border.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morice-line.jpg" alt="Morice Line" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saber68 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ligne_Morice.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
